      "created_at": "2021-02-17T23:30:23Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-02-17T23:30:23Z",
      "body": "It seems like it makes the most sense to have the us-privacy string as the canonical value, and check GPC in one place only, then write us-privacy as appropriate given the GPC value. The publisher can do this, since they already have to set us-privacy when the \"Do Not Sell\" link on the page is clicked.",
